=== Beta calibration result ===
converged                = true (2 sweeps, 24 solves, 490.2 s)
beta                       = 0.9876115514
bbar                       = -0.1758088830
qSav / qBorr / qGov (given) = 0.983574 / 0.983574 / 0.983574
pSS / pHH (given)           = 0.888297 / 0.758929   (piH = 0.316642)

moment                                          model       target    residual
median assets / mean labor income          1.18396144   1.18384681    1.15e-04
true borrowing limit / mean labor income   0.18499984   0.18500000   -1.62e-07
share negative liquid assets               0.04419345 not targeted          --
share hand-to-mouth (= piH by construction)   0.31664206   0.31664206   -2.35e-12
mean assets / mean labor income            1.70897827 not targeted          --

PV(Y) - PV(C) - PV(G)    = 3.170e-07   (exact identity when q = qGov)
government budget residual = 5.206e-09

Note the `WARNING: upper bound is binding` in the solver log. At the calibrated point a mass share of `3.87e-7` sits exactly at `aMax = 15`, with zero slack. The share is far too small to move the targeted moments, but `aMax` is touching and should be raised before using this calibration for anything sensitive to theright tail of the asset distribution.


# 2. Equilibrium computation
The calibrated instruments are used to compute the equilibrium of the model. The transcript below is reproducible: after the Section 1 setup it is the output of `run_history_independent_tax()`,

```
result_run = run_history_independent_tax(
                          J = 47, nZ = 15, nEps = 11, nKappa = 5, nA = 151,
                          beta  = result_calib.beta,
                          qSav  = 1/1.0167,
                          qBorr = 1/1.0167,
                          qGov  = 1/1.0167,
                          bbar  = result_calib.bbar,
                          aMax  = 50.0)

