# 3. Plotting
The following command produces a series of plots illustrating the equilibrium distributions, policy functions, and other relevant statistics. The plots are saved in the `figures/` directory.

```
include("plot_history_independent_tax.jl")
figs   = plot_history_independent_tax(result_run)

=== Figures saved ===
asset grid                = ~/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Projects/HSV_HistoryDep_LifeCycle/code/julia/Bewley/hi/figures/asset_grid.png
average assets by age     = ~/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Projects/HSV_HistoryDep_LifeCycle/code/julia/Bewley/hi/figures/average_assets_by_age.png
average hours by age      = ~/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Projects/HSV_HistoryDep_LifeCycle/code/julia/Bewley/hi/figures/average_hours_by_age.png
assets                    = ~/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Projects/HSV_HistoryDep_LifeCycle/code/julia/Bewley/hi/figures/unconditional_assets.png
hours worked              = ~/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Projects/HSV_HistoryDep_LifeCycle/code/julia/Bewley/hi/figures/unconditional_hours_worked.png
consumption               = ~/Library/CloudStorage/Dropbox/Projects/HSV_HistoryDep_LifeCycle/code/julia/Bewley/hi/figures/unconditional_consumption.png
```

# 4. Shutting down HtM
Modify the parameters to shut down hand-to-mouth people

```
result_run = run_history_independent_tax(
                          J = 79, nZ = 15, nEps = 11, nKappa = 5, nA = 151,
                          beta  = result_calib.beta,
                          qSav  = 1/1.0167,
                          qBorr = 1/1.0167,
                          qGov  = 1/1.0167,
                          bbar  = result_calib.bbar,
                          aMax  = 50.0,
                          pSS   = 1.0, pHH = 0.0)

